WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.959 --> 00:00:14.960
mother was busy writing a letter when her servant interrupted.

2
00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:17.020
"You have a visitor."

3
00:00:18.261 --> 00:00:20.921
The maid's eyes were wide with excitement.

4
00:00:20.941 --> 00:00:24.222
"It's the Earl of Dorincourt!"

5
00:00:27.683 --> 00:00:30.264
Mrs. Errol entered the main room of the cottage.

6
00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:34.422
A fierce-looking man was standing by the fireplace.

7
00:00:34.442 --> 00:00:41.566
"Mrs. Errol The earl paused to look into her eyes, which reminded him of Cedric's.

8
00:00:41.586 --> 00:00:46.728
"Your son looks so much like you."

9
00:00:46.748 --> 00:00:50.911
"People often say that," she said.

10
00:00:50.931 --> 00:00:54.313
"But I like to think he also resembles his father."

11
00:00:54.333 --> 00:00:58.615
"Yes," the earl hesitantly agreed.

12
00:01:00.948 --> 00:01:02.830
"He he is like my son too."

13
00:01:05.012 --> 00:01:08.094
Mrs. Errol took a seat on one side of the fireplace.

14
00:01:08.114 --> 00:01:10.937
"Please sit down, my lord."

15
00:01:12.919 --> 00:01:15.001
The earl was too agitated to sit.

16
00:01:15.961 --> 00:01:19.865
But he was impressed that she didn't seem troubled by his sudden arrival.

17
00:01:19.885 --> 00:01:23.288
"Do you know why I'm here?"

18
00:01:23.788 --> 00:01:24.529
he asked.

19
00:01:24.549 --> 00:01:31.405
"Mr. Havisham has told me that a woman—" "I've come to say that her claims will be investigated

20
00:01:31.485 --> 00:01:33.886
and challenged," the earl jumped in.

21
00:01:33.906 --> 00:01:37.367
"Your son's rights will be protected."

22
00:01:37.387 --> 00:01:42.748
"Cedric must have nothing that's not legally his," Mrs.

23
00:01:42.908 --> 00:01:44.609
Errol said in a soft voice.

24
00:01:46.289 --> 00:01:48.710
The earl waved his hand dismissively.

25
00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:54.292
"That outrageous woman and her child—" Mrs.

26
00:01:54.472 --> 00:01:55.372
Errol shrugged.

27
00:01:56.376 --> 00:01:59.899
"Perhaps she cares for her son as much as I care for Cedric, my lord."

28
00:02:00.959 --> 00:02:03.401
Mrs. Errol was respectful but firm.

29
00:02:04.522 --> 00:02:07.464
The earl noticed again that she was not intimidated.

30
00:02:08.565 --> 00:02:12.527
It reminded him of how unafraid Cedric had been when they first met.

31
00:02:13.768 --> 00:02:15.109
Mrs. Errol went on.

32
00:02:15.129 --> 00:02:20.333
"If this woman is your older son's wife, then her son is Lord Fauntleroy.

33
00:02:21.273 --> 00:02:22.354
And mine is not."

34
00:02:23.455 --> 00:02:24.716
The earl frowned.

35
00:02:25.956 --> 00:02:30.538
"I suppose you'd prefer that Cedric not be the Earl of Dorincourt."

36
00:02:31.658 --> 00:02:35.400
Mrs. Errol's face turned red, and she looked away for a moment.

37
00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:39.242
"It's a wonderful thing to be the Earl of Dorincourt.

38
00:02:40.382 --> 00:02:46.184
But it's more important that Cedric be like his father—brave, honest, and kind."

39
00:02:47.645 --> 00:02:49.426
The earl smiled slightly.

40
00:02:49.446 --> 00:02:54.528
"In contrast to what I have been, eh?"

41
00:02:56.680 --> 00:03:01.984
"I haven't had the pleasure of knowing you, but I know that my son believes—" Mrs.

42
00:03:02.105 --> 00:03:04.026
Errol looked directly at the earl.

43
00:03:04.046 --> 00:03:07.189
"I know that Cedric loves you."

44
00:03:07.209 --> 00:03:14.695
"Would he love me if you'd revealed why I never allowed you to visit the castle?"

45
00:03:14.715 --> 00:03:19.639
"No, and that's exactly why I never told him."

46
00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:24.122
The earl was momentarily stunned by her reply.

47
00:03:26.688 --> 00:03:29.649
"Well well, most people would have told him."

48
00:03:31.289 --> 00:03:33.110
He started to pace the room again.

49
00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:37.831
"When Cedric arrived, I was tired of my life.

50
00:03:38.812 --> 00:03:41.072
But he has given me something to live for.

51
00:03:42.153 --> 00:03:45.974
I'd be proud for him to succeed me as head of the family."

52
00:03:47.354 --> 00:03:49.475
The earl stopped right in front of Mrs.

53
00:03:49.575 --> 00:03:53.916
Errol. On the verge of tears, he said, "I am miserable!

54
00:03:55.028 --> 00:03:58.290
And it's because I'm miserable that I've come to you."

55
00:03:59.671 --> 00:04:03.913
Mrs. Errol noted that his hands were shaking and his voice was unsteady.

56
00:04:05.874 --> 00:04:07.455
She waited for him to go on.

57
00:04:07.475 --> 00:04:12.658
"I used to hate you, and I was jealous of you."

58
00:04:14.399 --> 00:04:19.042
Some of the earl's usual authority returned before he started to break down again.

59
00:04:19.062 --> 00:04:22.904
"This terrible business has changed all that.

60
00:04:24.192 --> 00:04:28.115
I'm here because Cedric loves you, and I love him.

61
00:04:29.276 --> 00:04:34.120
I've treated you badly, so I don't deserve any kindness from you.

62
00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:41.125
But treat me as well as you can, for Cedric's sake."

63
00:04:41.145 --> 00:04:43.366
Mrs. Errol was touched by his remarks.

64
00:04:45.428 --> 00:04:48.430
She stood up and moved the other chair closer to the earl.

65
00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:50.452
"I wish you would sit."

66
00:04:51.836 --> 00:04:54.739
She placed a reassuring hand on the earl's arm.

67
00:04:54.759 --> 00:04:58.442
"You're upset, and you need all your strength."

68
00:04:59.803 --> 00:05:04.346
The earl allowed her to help him sit, but he wiggled uncomfortably in the chair.

69
00:05:04.366 --> 00:05:07.449
"May I place a pillow behind your back?"

70
00:05:07.749 --> 00:05:08.990
Mrs. Errol asked.

71
00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:11.472
"That might make you feel better."

72
00:05:14.254 --> 00:05:17.397
She took a small pillow from the sofa and slipped it into place.

73
00:05:18.778 --> 00:05:20.960
The earl gave a nod and a quick smile.

74
00:05:22.252 --> 00:05:26.135
He was strangely comforted by this woman with the soothing voice and manner.

75
00:05:27.616 --> 00:05:32.160
Mrs. Errol was a good listener, which led him to talk even more about Cedric.

76
00:05:33.441 --> 00:05:35.403
Soon the earl was feeling much better.

77
00:05:35.423 --> 00:05:38.165
"This is a cheerful room.

78
00:05:39.146 --> 00:05:40.287
Do you like this house?"

79
00:05:40.847 --> 00:05:41.528
he asked.

80
00:05:42.568 --> 00:05:44.050
"Very much," Mrs.

81
00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:44.830
Errol said.

82
00:05:44.850 --> 00:05:48.433
"I couldn't ask for a lovelier house and garden."

83
00:05:48.453 --> 00:05:51.415
"And you, Mrs.

84
00:05:51.516 --> 00:05:55.117
Errol, are a lovely person," the earl thought.

85
00:05:55.137 --> 00:05:58.919
"Cedric is lucky that you're his mother."

86
00:06:00.259 --> 00:06:02.580
He wasn't ready to say those words aloud.

87
00:06:03.941 --> 00:06:08.843
Instead he said, "May I come again to talk over this matter?"

88
00:06:08.863 --> 00:06:13.145
"You're welcome here as often as you like, my lord."

89
00:06:14.425 --> 00:06:16.446
Mrs. Errol smiled brightly.

90
00:06:16.466 --> 00:06:20.188
"I'm always happy to talk about Cedric!"
